<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sarajevo</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Sarajevo is the principal city of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bosnia">Bosnia</a>, which came under Austro-Hungarian administration in 1878 and was annexed in 1908. On 28 June 1914 the heir to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/habsburg-dynasty">Habsburg</a> throne, Archduke <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/archduke-franz-ferdinand-of-austria">Franz Ferdinand</a>, was assassinated there by the Bosnian Serb nationalist <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gavrilo-princip">Gavrilo Princip</a>. Accounts of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/austro-hungarian-empire">Austro-Hungarian Empire</a> identify the assassination as the trigger of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/july-crisis">July Crisis</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/first-world-war">First World War</a>, which destroyed the empire.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sarajevo.jpg" alt="Sarajevo" width="320" height="191" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Julian Nyča · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sarajevo_City_Panorama.JPG" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
